  "question": {
    "text": "A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>M</mi></math> at rest disintegrates into two particles of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>M</mi></math>, respectively, having non zero velocities. The ratio of de-Broglie wavelength of particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> to that of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>M</mi></math> will be:",
